{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111WoML6GEqM5GS68fLwb9K","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tPAYLOAD 18/32: federation/server.py facade, model_currency.py (new), pii_patterns.py, plan_paths.py (new), policy.py facade, policy_preprocessors.py, secret_patterns.py.\n2\t\n3\tDECLARED CONDITIONS CHECKED AGAINST THE CODE\n4\t- Condition 4 (secret redactor offsets) is TRUE.\n5\t  - In secret_patterns.py:989-1000, scan() first matches the NFKC view, the same frame as before. Matches from that view are mapped back to positions in the original text by _map_to_original (lines 896-904). The original text is then scanned as a second frame. Every Finding indexes the text passed in.\n6\t  - _nfkc_segments (lines 821-870) checks at runtime that the per-segment NFKC images join up to NFKC(text). If they do not, it falls back to one segment covering the whole text, so the error is over-redaction, never a leak.\n7\t  - I traced the cases by hand: an ellipsis before an AKIA key, full-width runs, and a combining mark after ASCII. In each, the mapped span covers exactly the secret or more.\n8\t  - redact() (lines 1024-1046) and scan_and_redact() (lines 1049-1067) cut that same text using the merged runs, with offsets clamped to the text.\n9\t  - pii_patterns.py:731-758 now merges overlapping spans into their union. Every caller passes spans found on the string being redacted: lines 506-508 and 845-856.\n10\t  - No hunk touches the pattern catalog (roughly lines 80-680).\n11\t  - The Known-open ingress caveat is in CHANGELOG lines 418-422, as declared.\n12\t- Condition 5, for the paths in this payload, is TRUE. check_arbitration_kernel.py:311 lists _lib/_policy_parts/**/*, line 332 lists model_currency.py and line 334 lists plan_paths.py.\n13\t- Condition 7, for policy.py and federation/server.py, is TRUE. Both keep their paths and import names, and the logic now lives in _policy_parts/ and _server_parts/.\n14\t- Condition 9, for model_currency.py, is TRUE and declared:\n15\t  - _ALLOWED and _FLOOR accept the family patterns described in CHANGELOG lines 150-176.\n16\t  - _RETIRED holds only claude-opus-4-1.\n17\t  - The VETO check in agent_frontmatter.py:259 still accepts the old closed list (`or actual in allowed`), so the change only widens what passes.\n18\t\n19\tMOVED-CODE REVIEW (no defect found)\n20\t- federation/server.py:375-441\n21\t  - _bind_function rebinds every extracted function and method to the facade's globals(). Patching names such as server._maybe_reload_peers, load_peers or _load_rate_limit therefore still reaches the moved methods.\n22\t  - Relative imports inside methods (from .handlers / from .replay) resolve through the facade's __package__.\n23\t  - Passing __closure__ keeps the __class__ cell. Functions nested inside methods inherit the rebound globals.\n24\t  - In the MRO, _HandlerAuth comes before BaseHTTPRequestHandler, so its timeout, parse_request, log_message and do_* overrides still win. The three mixins define no method twice. __all__ is kept.\n25\t  - I checked the 11-gate order in handler_write.py:5-181 line by line against the removed text: it is identical.\n26\t  - Federation is off by default, and no hook imports server.py.\n27\t- policy.py:127-131\n28\t  - The parts are executed in the facade's own namespace, so their globals are identical to before. loading.py restores __all__.\n29\t  - Only policy_dispatch.py:46 (which catches Exception) and policy-shadow-runner import policy.py. The shipped settings template does not register policy_dispatch.\n30\t- Standard library only and Python 3.9 compatible across all seven files: FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure), nonlocal, bisect and typing aliases. No module in _lib shadows the standard library when model_currency.py runs as a script (validate-governance.sh:721).\n31\t- install.sh:1520-1549 copies _lib/ entries by glob, so the new _policy_parts/ and _server_parts/ directories ship.\n32\t\n33\tNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n34\t- None at P1.\n35\t\n36\tP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n37\t1. P2, secret_patterns.py:991-999 and :974; codex_egress_redact.py:104-105.\n38\t   - Problem: when the text changes under NFKC, scan() runs _scan_frame twice, and each run gets its own budget_seconds timer. _map_to_original runs between the two with no timer. Worst-case time is therefore about twice the budget, but the docstring still calls budget_seconds \"ITIMER wall-clock budget\", and codex_egress_redact still says it is \"bounded by budget_seconds=0.5\".\n39\t   - Scenario: crafted input to the check_adversary Bash pre-hook or to egress redaction takes up to about 1.0 s instead of 0.5 s.\n40\t   - Minimal fix: give the second frame only the time left in a shared deadline, or document that the budget applies per frame.\n41\t2. P2, policy_preprocessors.py:315 and plan_paths.py:13-15.\n42\t   - Problem: the old regex `PLAN-\\d{3}-[a-z0-9-]+\\.md$` matched names with doubled or trailing hyphens. The new grammar does not, so the plan-edit lifecycle policy no longer checks those files. check_budget.py:155 and check_ledger_checkpoint.py:283 still treat them as plans. The CHANGELOG (line 332) mentions only the FOLLOWUP widening.\n43\t   - Mitigation: validate_governance_fast.py:205 already reports such names as plan_schema_filename errors.\n44\t   - Minimal fix: add one CHANGELOG line, or make check_budget.py:155 use plan_paths.PLAN_FILENAME_RE.\n45\t3. P2 (wording), policy.py:126.\n46\t   - Problem: the comment \"Opt-out: CEO_POLICY_ENGINE_DISABLE=1 reverts to Python-hook fallback\" sits on the line that installs the parts. The switch is read only at policy_dispatch.py:128, after policy.py, and so the parts, have already been imported. The switch does not stop the parts from loading.\n47\t   - Minimal fix: reword the comment or move it to policy_dispatch.py.\n48\t4. P2, model_currency.py:4 and :41-44.\n49\t   - Problem: the _RETIRED check runs before the explicit list. An adopter who lists claude-opus-4-1 in availableModels now gets settings_tamper_model_remap from effective_config.py:482, and the tier-policy loader rejects that id, where exact membership used to pass. This is declared in CHANGELOG line 173 and the model is retired.\n50\t   - Separately: the predicate's families leave out claude-fable-*, while the maintainer smoke script (scripts/local/smoke-install-parity.sh:107, out of scope) accepts claude-fable-[5-9]*. This is not a regression, since the old closed list had the same limit, but the two have drifted apart.\n51\t   - Minimal fix: align the smoke harness with the predicate, or add a Fable row to the predicate.\n52\t\n53\tVERDICT: GO Conditions 4, 5, 7 and 9 hold for the code in this payload, the two moved modules keep their behavior, Python stays standard-library only and 3.9 compatible, and I found no P0 or P1, only four P2 follow-ups.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a25f8a7-7747-4a27-bd7f-b0b8e6b81433","uuid":"2b5d5f5e-1a24-4346-8e67-da2514785223","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:10:15.893Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-18.verdict.txt","content":"PAYLOAD 18/32: federation/server.py facade, model_currency.py (new), pii_patterns.py, plan_paths.py (new), policy.py facade, policy_preprocessors.py, secret_patterns.py.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS CHECKED AGAINST THE CODE\n- Condition 4 (secret redactor offsets) is TRUE.\n  - In secret_patterns.py:989-1000, scan() first matches the NFKC view, the same frame as before. Matches from that view are mapped back to positions in the original text by _map_to_original (lines 896-904). The original text is then scanned as a second frame. Every Finding indexes the text passed in.\n  - _nfkc_segments (lines 821-870) checks at runtime that the per-segment NFKC images join up to NFKC(text). If they do not, it falls back to one segment covering the whole text, so the error is over-redaction, never a leak.\n  - I traced the cases by hand: an ellipsis before an AKIA key, full-width runs, and a combining mark after ASCII. In each, the mapped span covers exactly the secret or more.\n  - redact() (lines 1024-1046) and scan_and_redact() (lines 1049-1067) cut that same text using the merged runs, with offsets clamped to the text.\n  - pii_patterns.py:731-758 now merges overlapping spans into their union. Every caller passes spans found on the string being redacted: lines 506-508 and 845-856.\n  - No hunk touches the pattern catalog (roughly lines 80-680).\n  - The Known-open ingress caveat is in CHANGELOG lines 418-422, as declared.\n- Condition 5, for the paths in this payload, is TRUE. check_arbitration_kernel.py:311 lists _lib/_policy_parts/**/*, line 332 lists model_currency.py and line 334 lists plan_paths.py.\n- Condition 7, for policy.py and federation/server.py, is TRUE. Both keep their paths and import names, and the logic now lives in _policy_parts/ and _server_parts/.\n- Condition 9, for model_currency.py, is TRUE and declared:\n  - _ALLOWED and _FLOOR accept the family patterns described in CHANGELOG lines 150-176.\n  - _RETIRED holds only claude-opus-4-1.\n  - The VETO check in agent_frontmatter.py:259 still accepts the old closed list (`or actual in allowed`), so the change only widens what passes.\n\nMOVED-CODE REVIEW (no defect found)\n- federation/server.py:375-441\n  - _bind_function rebinds every extracted function and method to the facade's globals(). Patching names such as server._maybe_reload_peers, load_peers or _load_rate_limit therefore still reaches the moved methods.\n  - Relative imports inside methods (from .handlers / from .replay) resolve through the facade's __package__.\n  - Passing __closure__ keeps the __class__ cell. Functions nested inside methods inherit the rebound globals.\n  - In the MRO, _HandlerAuth comes before BaseHTTPRequestHandler, so its timeout, parse_request, log_message and do_* overrides still win. The three mixins define no method twice. __all__ is kept.\n  - I checked the 11-gate order in handler_write.py:5-181 line by line against the removed text: it is identical.\n  - Federation is off by default, and no hook imports server.py.\n- policy.py:127-131\n  - The parts are executed in the facade's own namespace, so their globals are identical to before. loading.py restores __all__.\n  - Only policy_dispatch.py:46 (which catches Exception) and policy-shadow-runner import policy.py. The shipped settings template does not register policy_dispatch.\n- Standard library only and Python 3.9 compatible across all seven files: FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure), nonlocal, bisect and typing aliases. No module in _lib shadows the standard library when model_currency.py runs as a script (validate-governance.sh:721).\n- install.sh:1520-1549 copies _lib/ entries by glob, so the new _policy_parts/ and _server_parts/ directories ship.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n- None at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. P2, secret_patterns.py:991-999 and :974; codex_egress_redact.py:104-105.\n   - Problem: when the text changes under NFKC, scan() runs _scan_frame twice, and each run gets its own budget_seconds timer. _map_to_original runs between the two with no timer. Worst-case time is therefore about twice the budget, but the docstring still calls budget_seconds \"ITIMER wall-clock budget\", and codex_egress_redact still says it is \"bounded by budget_seconds=0.5\".\n   - Scenario: crafted input to the check_adversary Bash pre-hook or to egress redaction takes up to about 1.0 s instead of 0.5 s.\n   - Minimal fix: give the second frame only the time left in a shared deadline, or document that the budget applies per frame.\n2. P2, policy_preprocessors.py:315 and plan_paths.py:13-15.\n   - Problem: the old regex `PLAN-\\d{3}-[a-z0-9-]+\\.md$` matched names with doubled or trailing hyphens. The new grammar does not, so the plan-edit lifecycle policy no longer checks those files. check_budget.py:155 and check_ledger_checkpoint.py:283 still treat them as plans. The CHANGELOG (line 332) mentions only the FOLLOWUP widening.\n   - Mitigation: validate_governance_fast.py:205 already reports such names as plan_schema_filename errors.\n   - Minimal fix: add one CHANGELOG line, or make check_budget.py:155 use plan_paths.PLAN_FILENAME_RE.\n3. P2 (wording), policy.py:126.\n   - Problem: the comment \"Opt-out: CEO_POLICY_ENGINE_DISABLE=1 reverts to Python-hook fallback\" sits on the line that installs the parts. The switch is read only at policy_dispatch.py:128, after policy.py, and so the parts, have already been imported. The switch does not stop the parts from loading.\n   - Minimal fix: reword the comment or move it to policy_dispatch.py.\n4. P2, model_currency.py:4 and :41-44.\n   - Problem: the _RETIRED check runs before the explicit list. An adopter who lists claude-opus-4-1 in availableModels now gets settings_tamper_model_remap from effective_config.py:482, and the tier-policy loader rejects that id, where exact membership used to pass. This is declared in CHANGELOG line 173 and the model is retired.\n   - Separately: the predicate's families leave out claude-fable-*, while the maintainer smoke script (scripts/local/smoke-install-parity.sh:107, out of scope) accepts claude-fable-[5-9]*. This is not a regression, since the old closed list had the same limit, but the two have drifted apart.\n   - Minimal fix: align the smoke harness with the predicate, or add a Fable row to the predicate.\n\nVERDICT: GO Conditions 4, 5, 7 and 9 hold for the code in this payload, the two moved modules keep their behavior, Python stays standard-library only and 3.9 compatible, and I found no P0 or P1, only four P2 follow-ups.\n","numLines":54,"startLine":1,"totalLines":54}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0111WoML6GEqM5GS68fLwb9K","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
