 agent_frontmatter.py:259 keeps `or actual in allowed`.\n    - effective_config.py:721 keeps `startswith(\"claude-\")`.\n    - validate-governance.sh:718 keeps the literal case list.\n\nMOVED CODE (no defect found)\n- Rebinding (server.py:375-419): `_bind_function` rebinds every extracted function and method to the facade's globals().\n  - Patching server.<name> still reaches the moved methods.\n  - The relative imports inside methods (`from .replay`, `from .handlers`) resolve through the facade's `__package__`.\n  - Nested closures (`_revert_inflight`, `_poll`, `_pii_redact_adapter`) inherit the rebound globals.\n  - No part uses super(), `__class__`, nonlocal or global, so no closure-cell mismatch is possible.\n- Class-level names: the only one, `timeout = HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`, is read from the snapshot at load. The old class attribute was also evaluated once.\n- MRO: _HandlerAuth comes before BaseHTTPRequestHandler, so its timeout, server_version, sys_version, parse_request, log_message and do_* overrides still win. The three mixins define no method twice. parse_request calls the base class explicitly.\n- Text checks against the removed code, all identical:\n  - the 11-gate order;\n  - the sigref regex and the 24 h TTL;\n  - the 1 MiB body cap and the 4096-byte GET read;\n  - the kill-switch values;\n  - rate-limit DEFAULT-DENY and AC6 redaction fail-closed;\n  - quarantine without revert in the reaper.\n- Reach: no production code imports server.py, and federation/__init__.py does not import it.\n- Install: install.sh:1520-1549 copies _lib/federation recursively, so _server_parts ships.\n- Python: standard library only and 3.9-compatible. That holds for FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure), the `__kwdefaults__` copy, the typing aliases in pii_patterns (Tuple is imported at :79), and plan_paths.\n- model_currency.py as a script: no module in _lib shadows the standard library when it runs that way (validate-governance.sh:721).\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n- None at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. P2, pii_patterns.py:731-758 against CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 254-272.\n   - Problem: the CHANGELOG's redactor section describes only secret_patterns. The PII union change is declared only in condition 4. It changes the redacted_text of check_output_safety.py:195-215 and of the federation audit-summary: more is redacted, and merged runs carry one family token.\n   - Minimal fix: add one CHANGELOG line.\n2. P2, plan_paths.py:13-23 against check_budget.py:155 (carried from the rc).\n   - The new grammar matches validate_governance_fast.py:63. It widens to FOLLOWUP names and Windows separators.\n   - It narrows to exclude doubled or trailing hyphens, and parents such as \"x.claude/plans\". check_plan_edit.py:240 and policy_preprocessors.py:315 therefore no longer gate those names, while check_budget.py:155 still treats them as plans.\n   - Mitigation: validate_governance_fast reports such names as schema errors.\n   - Minimal fix: make check_budget use plan_paths.PLAN_FILENAME_RE, and add a CHANGELOG line for the narrowing.\n3. P2, server.py:400-414 and _server_parts/handler_auth.py:11.\n   - Problem: when a part is missing (partial install), _load_part lets FileNotFoundError out of exec_module instead of ImportError. Separately, `_server_parts/` is an importable package, but importing handler_auth directly raises NameError (HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS).\n   - Impact: no production importer exists, and a federation server that cannot import does not start, which is the safe direction for a network listener.\n   - Minimal fix: in _load_part, raise ImportError when `_location.is_file()` is false, and drop `__init__.py` or document that the parts are not importable alone.\n4. P2, model_currency.py:7-8 and :11-16.\n   - Problem: the Fable line is admitted only through two legacy ids, and only when no explicit list is passed. A newer Fable id such as claude-fable-5-2 is refused by validate-governance.sh:721 and by tier_policy_cli/_types.py:35 unless listed. In effective_config.py:482 it is flagged as settings_tamper_model_remap unless it is in the ADR-149 set.\n   - This is not a regression: the old closed list had the same limit. But the \"currency\" predicate does not follow the newest family, while the out-of-scope smoke harness admits claude-fable-[5-9]*.\n   - Minimal fix: add a Fable family row, or align the harness.\n5. P2 (wording), comment headers left detached from their code:\n   - server.py:363-366, the \"Rate limiter — joint key\" header;\n   - the trailing headers at the end of configuration.py (\"Request handler\"), handler_auth.py (\"Wave D 11-gate write dispatcher\"), handler_write.py (\"Gate #9\"), handler_read.py (\"AC6 fail-CLOSED contract.\") and redaction.py (\"FederationServer — orchestrator\").\n   - Minimal fix: move each header next to its code, or delete it.","decision":"GO","sentence":"No declared condition this payload touches (4, 5, 7, 9) is false against the code, and I found no P0 or new P1: the federation facade keeps globals, patch points, MRO and the 11-gate fail-closed text unchanged, the PII union only adds redaction, and the new model and plan-path predicates match what the CHANGELOG declares, leaving only P2 follow-ups."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3834,"cache_read_input_tokens":169000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3834},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a25f8a7-7747-4a27-bd7f-b0b8e6b81433","uuid":"ea598cdb-7faa-49af-8399-04bc291750b5","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:15:53.202Z","request_id":"req_011Ch79BTAA7KjDqGxZ9VNMK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HAr8vX626Av9BZDsgiQgkT":{"report":"PAYLOAD 19/34. Files: federation/